Half-open interval model [start, end) per docs/audit/INTEGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md:107, with UTC
instant + IANA zone per :106. Shape:

  export interface TimeInterval {
    readonly startUtc: string;   // ISO-8601 instant, UTC
    readonly endUtc: string;
    readonly timeZone: string;   // IANA, e.g. "Europe/Berlin"
  }

  export type IntervalViolation = "empty" | "reversed";

  export function validateInterval(i: TimeInterval): readonly IntervalViolation[];
  export function overlaps(a: TimeInterval, b: TimeInterval): boolean;

Invariants (plan lines 233-235): start==end invalid ("empty"); end<start rejected ("reversed")
while night work is not an approved model; duration AND overlap use the SAME model, so adjacent
intervals 08:00-10:00 / 10:00-12:00 do not overlap.

No Date-object mutation, no timezone library, no I/O — only Date.parse / arithmetic on the ISO
strings. Note `readonly IntervalViolation[]` as the return type rather than throwing: the domain
reports, the command boundary in apps/api decides. Keep it exception-free so the same function
serves the optimistic client-side UX check (INTEGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md:110 — client feedback is
never authority) and the authoritative server re-validation (:108).

Deterministic capacity per (employee, planning week). Plan lines 248-253 require the week rule
and timezone to be written down explicitly — proposal Europe/Berlin + ISO-8601 week, to be pinned
in ADR-002. Two separate weeks must not produce a shared conflict; a capacity warning is NOT a
publish blocker; the four-week projection reuses the same weekly values as the week view.

  export interface CapacityWindow {
    readonly isoYear: number;
    readonly isoWeek: number;   // 1..53
    readonly minutesPlanned: number;
    readonly minutesContracted: number;
  }
  export function weeklyCapacity(
    intervals: readonly TimeInterval[],
    contractedMinutesPerWeek: number,
  ): readonly CapacityWindow[];

ISO week 52/53/01 rollover and DST boundaries must be pure functions here (plan line 253), which
is only possible because the model stores UTC instants plus the IANA zone rather than local
wall-clock strings.

