## The mechanism: repositories are *created inside* the transaction, so they cannot exist outside it

The weak version of AC1 is "repository takes a `Transaction<DB>`". That is not enough. Kysely's own `Transaction<DB>` already is nominal (`kysely@0.28.17` `dist/cjs/kysely.d.ts:409-417`: `class Transaction<DB> extends Kysely<DB>` with `#private` and `get isTransaction(): true`), so a plain `Kysely<DB>` cannot be passed. But `Transaction<DB>` proves *"a transaction"*, never *"a tenant context was set and verified"*. Both are needed.

The strong version: **the application layer never receives a database handle at all.** Repositories are constructed by the UnitOfWork *after* the context probe succeeded, handed to the caller's callback, and revoked in `finally`.

```ts
// apps/api/src/platform/database/unit-of-work.ts  — ONE file on purpose:
// the construction token must never be importable.
import { Kysely, Transaction, sql } from "kysely";
import type { DB } from "./database.types";

/** Modul-privat. Verlaesst diese Datei nie. Kein export. */
const OPEN = Symbol("TenantTransaction.open");

export interface TenantPrincipal {
  /** JWT `sub` — Identitaet AUSSCHLIESSLICH aus verifiziertem Token. */
  readonly userId: string;
  /** Der EINE Mandant dieses Requests. */
  readonly orgId: string;
}

export class TenantContextError extends Error {}

/**
 * Nominal gebrandeter, laufzeitgepruefter Transaktionsgriff.
 * Vorbild: packages/domain/src/time-interval.ts:107-134 — private Felder
 * machen den Typ nominal, und die Invariante steht im KONSTRUKTOR, weil
 * `private constructor` beim Emit geloescht wird.
 */
export class TenantTransaction {
  readonly #trx: Transaction<DB>;
  readonly #orgId: string;
  readonly #userId: string;
  #open = true;                     // #private ist keine Property: Object.freeze beruehrt es nicht

  constructor(token: symbol, trx: Transaction<DB>, orgId: string, userId: string) {
    if (token !== OPEN) {
      throw new TypeError(
        "TenantTransaction entsteht ausschliesslich in UnitOfWork.runInTenant(). " +
          "Ein direkt konstruiertes Objekt haette keinen verifizierten Tenantkontext.",
      );
    }
    this.#trx = trx; this.#orgId = orgId; this.#userId = userId;
    Object.freeze(this);
  }

  get orgId(): string { this.#assertOpen(); return this.#orgId; }
  get userId(): string { this.#assertOpen(); return this.#userId; }

  /** Jede Tabellenlese ist bereits auf DIESEN Mandanten eingeschraenkt. */
  from<T extends TenantTable>(table: T) {
    this.#assertOpen();
    return this.#trx.selectFrom(table).where(`${table}.org_id`, "=", this.#orgId);
  }

  /** Jeder Insert traegt org_id — der Aufrufer kann ihn nicht setzen. */
  insertInto<T extends TenantTable>(table: T, values: TenantInsert<T>) {
    this.#assertOpen();
    return this.#trx.insertInto(table).values({ ...values, org_id: this.#orgId });
  }

  updateIn<T extends TenantTable>(table: T) {
    this.#assertOpen();
    return this.#trx.updateTable(table).where(`${table}.org_id`, "=", this.#orgId);
  }

  /**
   * AK 5 — der DOKUMENTIERTE Escape Hatch. Nimmt ausdruecklich KEINEN string,
   * sondern nur ein `sql`-Template: Parametrisierung ist damit die einzige
   * bauliche Moeglichkeit, nicht die empfohlene.
   */
  executeRaw<R>(query: RawBuilder<R>): Promise<QueryResult<R>> {
    this.#assertOpen();
    return query.execute(this.#trx);
  }

  /** @internal — nur unit-of-work.ts ruft das auf. */
  revoke(token: symbol): void { if (token === OPEN) this.#open = false; }

  #assertOpen(): void {
    if (!this.#open) {
      throw new TenantContextError(
        "TenantTransaction ist geschlossen. Der Griff wurde ueber runInTenant() hinaus " +
          "benutzt — die Pooler-Connection gehoert inzwischen einem anderen Mandanten.",
      );
    }
  }
}

export class UnitOfWork {
  constructor(private readonly db: Kysely<DB>) {}

  async runInTenant<T>(
    principal: TenantPrincipal,
    work: (tx: TenantTransaction) => Promise<T>,
  ): Promise<T> {
    return this.db.transaction().execute(async (trx) => {
      // 1) Kontext TRANSAKTIONSLOKAL — woertlich das Muster aus
      //    apps/api/test/tenant-context.helper.ts:53-57. Kein Variant.
      await sql`select set_config('request.jwt.claims', ${JSON.stringify({
        sub: principal.userId,
        role: "authenticated",
      })}, true)`.execute(trx);
      await sql`set local role authenticated`.execute(trx);

      // 2) VERIFIKATION (siehe contextVerification) — eigene Anweisung.
      await assertTenantContext(trx, principal);

      // 3) Erst JETZT existiert ein Griff. Vorher gibt es keinen.
      const tx = new TenantTransaction(OPEN, trx, principal.orgId, principal.userId);
      try {
        return await work(tx);
      } finally {
        tx.revoke(OPEN);   // entwerteter Griff: jede spaetere Nutzung wirft
      }
    });
  }
}
```

Repositories then look like this, and there is **no other constructor path**:

```ts
// apps/api/src/modules/planning/infrastructure/assignment.repository.ts
export class AssignmentRepository implements AssignmentRepositoryPort {
  constructor(private readonly tx: TenantTransaction) {}   // nur so erreichbar
  ...
}

// application sieht nie einen DB-Griff, nur Ports:
export interface PlanningUnitOfWork {
  run<T>(p: TenantPrincipal, work: (repos: PlanningRepositories) => Promise<T>): Promise<T>;
}
```

The infrastructure adapter builds `PlanningRepositories` from the `TenantTransaction` *inside* `runInTenant`. Result: **there is no expression in the codebase that yields a repository outside a verified tenant transaction** — not because a rule forbids writing one, but because the only value that can produce one is created after the probe and revoked before the transaction ends.

## Judgement on the four options you asked about

| Option | Verdict |
|---|---|
| Pass the transaction as the only way to obtain a repository | **Primary mechanism.** Strongest: removes the illegal state instead of detecting it. |
| Branded type (`#private`, like `TimeInterval`) | **Yes, as the carrier.** `time-interval.ts:107-134` is the exact precedent; note its own comment at :111-121 — `private constructor` is erased at emit, so the guard must be a *runtime* token check, not a TS modifier. |
