  env: { EASYTREE_TENANT_TESTS: required, EASYTREE_TEST_DB_URL: postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres }
  run: |
    pnpm --filter @easytree/api exec vitest run test/tenant-unit-of-work.integration.test.ts 2>&1 | tee /tmp/uow-direct.log
    grep -E "\[tenant-uow\] mode=required target=direct executed=[1-9][0-9]* skipped=0" /tmp/uow-direct.log
- name: UnitOfWork tenant gate (fail-closed, TRANSACTION POOLER)
  env: { EASYTREE_TENANT_TESTS: required }        # EASYTREE_TEST_POOLER_URL kommt aus ci.yml:193
  run: |
    pnpm --filter @easytree/api exec vitest run test/tenant-unit-of-work.integration.test.ts 2>&1 | tee /tmp/uow-pooled.log
    grep -E "\[tenant-uow\] mode=required target=pooler executed=[1-9][0-9]* skipped=0" /tmp/uow-pooled.log
```

`EASYTREE_TEST_POOLER_URL` is already exported into `GITHUB_ENV` by the pre-flight step (`ci.yml:193`), and the workspace deps are already built by `ci.yml:121-122`. **No new job** — so `scripts/setup-branch-protection.sh` (which drift-checks `ci.yml`'s job list against `REQUIRED_CHECKS` in *both* directions, `:98-124`) stays satisfied and the ruleset needs no admin re-apply. This is the same choice EYT-46 made (`CLAUDE.md:215-216`; `docs/plans/2026-07-26-eyt-sprint-3-integrierter-slice.md:222`).

A companion fail-closed regression proof in the shape of `apps/api/test/tenant-gate.fail-closed.test.ts:12-38` (spawn a child vitest with an unreachable URL, assert non-zero exit and `fail-closed` in the output) should cover the new suite too — otherwise the new gate is the one gate nobody proved can go red.

